---
import ContentLayout from '@/layouts/ContentLayout.astro';

const breadcrumbs = [{ name: 'Privacy Policy', url: '/privacy-policy' }];
---

<ContentLayout
  title="Privacy Policy | LIC Calculator"
  description="Privacy Policy and data protection practices for lic-calculators.com."
  pageTitle="Privacy Policy"
  pageSubtitle="Last updated: August 2026"
  breadcrumbs={breadcrumbs}
>
  <div class="space-y-6 text-sm text-slate-700 leading-relaxed">
    <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-slate-900">1. Information We Collect</h2>
    <p>
      lic-calculators.com is committed to protecting your privacy. Our calculators run directly in your browser or through stateless API requests. We do <strong>NOT</strong> store your policy numbers, personal identity numbers, or banking credentials.
    </p>

    <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-slate-900">2. Calculation Inputs</h2>
    <p>
      Numerical parameters entered into calculators (such as age, sum assured, term, and premiums) are processed to compute results and are not linked to identifiable personal records.
    </p>

    <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-slate-900">3. Analytics & Cookies</h2>
    <p>
      We may use privacy-preserving web analytics to evaluate traffic volume and improve calculator performance without tracking personal identities.
    </p>

    <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-slate-900">4. Third-Party Links</h2>
    <p>
      Our website may contain references or links to official portals (such as licindia.in). We are not responsible for the privacy practices of external websites.
    </p>
  </div>
</ContentLayout>
